sequenceDiagram
    participant USER as User process<br/>(target binary)
    participant K as Kernel uprobes
    participant BPF as BPF program
    participant LD as libbpf at attach

    Note over USER,LD: One-time attach
    LD->>K: open /usr/bin/bash<br/>find symbol readline at offset 0x4f200
    LD->>K: register uprobe at inode+offset
    K->>K: insert breakpoint (int3) at first instruction<br/>via /proc/self/mem-style write
    Note over K: All processes loading<br/>/usr/bin/bash get the breakpoint<br/>(via copy-on-write on first execute)

    Note over USER,BPF: Runtime — every readline() call
    USER->>USER: bash calls readline(prompt)
    USER->>USER: int3 trap fires!
    USER->>K: kernel handles trap
    K->>BPF: invoke uprobe BPF program with pt_regs
    BPF->>BPF: read prompt from RDI<br/>via bpf_probe_read_user_str
    BPF-->>K: return
    K->>K: emulate the original instruction
    K-->>USER: resume readline()
